Z||000000||MickeyAsh||07-22-2001||03:35 PM||||I'm looking for a vendor that either already makes or can produce an etched glass decal about 6 - 8 inches high, that would either be that Pegasus logo alone, or that with "Fiero" etched on over it... I was wondering if you guys could point me in the right direction.... TIA.||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||07-22-2001||07:18 PM||||cut glass[sandblasted] is a arts craft that a buddy does but he got hot and is very pricie now.he does fish mostly but is booked for the future anyway.<BR> i don't know of never heard of a decal that is etched but cut glass is very good looking art.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||07-22-2001||07:45 PM||||I used to do that a lot on custom vans. I just used an electric engraver. you can draw or trace your pic on paper and tape it on the window (inside if its tinted, outside if it clear) just trace the lines. If you have areas to fill in with texture you can buy a small sandblaster gun at auto paint store for around $25. use masking tape over areas you dont want filled in. Another trick is to brush or spray some paint in the engraving then scrape it off with razor blade and steelwool. (ie- gold in etching on a black car)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe Torma||07-22-2001||08:34 PM||||Are you talking about the simulated etched glass vinyl?  I could probably help you with that...can you give me a rough layout of it?<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||07-22-2001||09:10 PM||||I saw on tv once on one of those home shows ,they were etching glas with some type of acid that can be bought at a craft store.The way I remember you put your stencil on the glass and you brush this gel on over it you wait a while ,rinse it off,and presto you have etched glass that you do your self sorta of inexpensivly.hope this might give you one more option.||||reg||3
Z||000005||MickeyAsh||07-22-2001||11:10 PM||||Allow me to be more specific, hehe... I'm actually looking to put the Fiero logo on a piece of Plexiglass that will then be in front of a showcased sub amplifier behind my driver seat... that might help in finding a solution...||||reg||1
Z||000006||Joe Torma||07-22-2001||11:49 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MickeyAsh:<BR><B>Allow me to be more specific, hehe... I'm actually looking to put the Fiero logo on a piece of Plexiglass that will then be in front of a showcased sub amplifier behind my driver seat... that might help in finding a solution...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok, either the vinyl or real etching/sandblasting will work.  The vinyl is easier (since you need it anyway for the etching)...just stick it on.  Oh, do it on the reverse side and be sure to illuminate the edges(neon or colored bulb) of the plexi...The pegasus will glow!<P><BR>Joe<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 07-22-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||MickeyAsh||07-23-2001||12:15 AM||||So what's the "Vinyl method"? lol And yeah, that was the whole idea behind the etching, to have the glowing pegasus over the amp... I thought it'd add a very nice custom look... I already have my high output red LEDs wired and ready for both sides of the plexi...    &gt;=)<p>[This message has been edited by MickeyAsh (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Joe Torma||07-23-2001||03:46 AM||||Ah...I knew what your were going to do!  It should look great!<P>The vinyl is called etch-lite and is pretty much a matte clear.  Basically you'll just need a size for the pegasus, and I can cut it(I have the logo prepared).  all you would have to do is apply the sticker.<P>I have a small sample of the vinyl and I will try it, to make sure it will "illuminate"  if it doesn't...my suggestion would be plain ol' white...it is sure to reflect the colored light.<P>Joe||||reg||1
